1
00:00:02,586 --> 00:00:05,172
Do you know what happened
to our parents?

2
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:06,797
I never met them.

3
00:00:06,798 --> 00:00:09,092
Maybe they died in the storm.

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,053
Or maybe they're still
out there...

5
00:00:12,054 --> 00:00:14,306
Ah, a mother's set.

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,226
It's the sigil of the artist
who made it,

7
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:18,602
a unique signature.

8
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:21,437
<i>Ha! The Faceless Queen!</i>

9
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:22,731
<i>This is huge!</i>

10
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:25,608
In the name of Ellora,
I arrest you!

11
00:00:25,609 --> 00:00:27,485
Calling any and all Havens.

12
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:30,239
<i>This is Ellora. We need you.</i>

13
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:37,412
The welcome mat
is rolled out

14
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:38,496
for the Haven Envoys.

15
00:00:38,497 --> 00:00:40,039
Agam is catering the Summit.

16
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,124
Her kachoris alone
might seal a deal.

17
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:44,043
- Have you--
- Assigned the Brigade's best

18
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:45,378
to handle security?

19
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:46,296
Done.

20
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:50,425
I think we might actually
be able to save Ellora.

21
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:53,345
We make quite a team.

22
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:57,766
Perhaps, uh, once this is done,
we can...

23
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:00,352
I'd like that.

24
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,312
Then it's a date.

25
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:04,771
We've just got to get through
the next few days...

26
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:10,988
Finally some service.

27
00:01:11,113 --> 00:01:12,823
Can I upgrade my room?

28
00:01:12,948 --> 00:01:14,324
Something for royalty.

29
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,618
Jae told us everything...

30
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:18,911
Zi.

31
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,247
Clever of you
to hide under Ellora.

32
00:01:21,248 --> 00:01:24,917
But not clever enough
to respect the Anomaly's power.

33
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:28,088
My people have survived worse.

34
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:29,880
You won't be rid of us
that easily.

35
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:33,134
Perhaps not,
but we know the Faceless

36
00:01:33,135 --> 00:01:34,469
won't make a single move

37
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:36,805
without their precious queen.

38
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,723
Tell us where they are,

39
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:40,392
and you have my word
I'll be lenient.

40
00:01:40,517 --> 00:01:44,312
Are you trying to negotiate?!

41
00:01:44,313 --> 00:01:45,563
Not your forte.

42
00:01:45,564 --> 00:01:47,691
How's this for negotiation?

43
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:50,192
If you don't tell me
what I want to know,

44
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:54,656
you'll never see your people
or the sun ever again.

45
00:01:57,034 --> 00:02:00,621
I'll do whatever it takes
for the survival of Ellora.

46
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:04,458
Leave the Queen to ponder
how heavy that crown is.

47
00:02:10,005 --> 00:02:11,464
Silly woman.

48
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,634
I'm not the one you need
to worry about.

49
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:18,013
<i>Fire.</i>

50
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:19,847
<i>Air.</i>

51
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:20,849
<i>Water.</i>

52
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:23,851
<i>Earth.</i>

53
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:28,272
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,
master of all four elements,</i>

54
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:30,359
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

55
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:32,152
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

56
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:34,904
<i>the world built
The Seven Havens.</i>

57
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:38,699
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,
but for the first time,</i>

58
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,618
<i>there are two.</i>

59
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:42,621
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again,</i>

60
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:46,166
<i>but I believe
they will save it.</i>

61
00:02:58,679 --> 00:03:00,722
It's the envoys
from New Ba Sing Se!

62
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:04,142
They live like
it's still ancient times.

63
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:06,268
Those folks are from Akasha...

64
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,853
the only people
who've figured out

65
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:09,272
how to use Old World tech.

66
00:03:10,107 --> 00:03:13,609
Hmm... I think that's
the Empress of Feather Mountain.

67
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:17,114
Karthik says she's a powerful
airbender, who everybody adores.

68
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:18,573
Must be nice.

69
00:03:19,241 --> 00:03:21,535
I'm the Avatar!

70
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,369
I should be bringing
the Envoys together,

71
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:24,788
helping save Ellora.

72
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:27,249
Instead I'm watching
from the rafters!

73
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:30,626
We get it,
you're the head of the class.

74
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:31,920
Catch!

75
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,886
Uh... Whoa-uh!

76
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:42,013
Ugh!

77
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:43,807
Huh?

78
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,307
My pudding!

79
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:50,271
Avatar,
master of all five elements!

80
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:53,442
Air, water, earth, fire...

81
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:55,067
And pudding!

82
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:04,410
But we need to consider
our own people.

83
00:04:04,411 --> 00:04:06,329
Would they call us
for no reason?

84
00:04:09,458 --> 00:04:10,208
Ugh!

85
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:11,710
Who are you--

86
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:14,837
Ssh! They're looking for me.

87
00:04:14,838 --> 00:04:18,047
Empress?
Empress, where did you go?

88
00:04:18,048 --> 00:04:19,801
Are they assassins?

89
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:21,385
Ugh. Worse.

90
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:22,720
Those are my guards.

91
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,346
They're pretty overprotective.

92
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:26,098
I just needed
some breathing room

93
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:27,516
and you looked...

94
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:30,854
well, just as out of place
as me.

95
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:33,189
Yeah, I'm a bit lost.

96
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:35,441
I've never been
to a summit before.

97
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:36,610
What do you do with your hands?

98
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:42,157
No idea. I just make
little tornadoes when I'm bored.

99
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,575
There you are, Empress.

100
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,034
We were worried sick.

101
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:46,660
Where did you get
that drink from?

102
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:49,371
Wait, did someone test this
for poison?!

103
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:52,375
Ugh!

104
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:58,631
So, you met Empress Yeshe?

105
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:01,342
Yeah, I guess so.

106
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:11,228
Oof!

107
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:16,775
Not again!

108
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:27,702
Take care of Kayoko.

109
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:36,711
Well, this is
certainly a surprise.

110
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,047
Nobuo, Tanushree, Rehan,

111
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:42,508
what are the Head Lotuses
of Akasha and New Ba doing here?

112
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:44,927
Rumors about the Avatar
reach a fever pitch

113
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:46,805
and you cut communications
with us?

114
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:48,974
That is a big no-no, Karthik.

115
00:05:49,099 --> 00:05:51,309
I didn't "cut" communications.

116
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:53,769
I've been dealing
with strange entities,

117
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,020
and the Faceless bandits.

118
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,313
Excuses!

119
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:57,732
Given your recent behavior,

120
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:01,318
we feel it's time
she faced The Trial.

121
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:03,362
Nisha is making good progress.

122
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,322
There's no need
for drastic action.

123
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,241
If she is doing so well,

124
00:06:07,242 --> 00:06:09,660
then why the sudden silence, hmm?

125
00:06:09,661 --> 00:06:12,247
I hate to say it,
but it sounds like

126
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:14,206
you might be hiding
something from us.

127
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,250
Hiding? I'm not...

128
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:18,670
...not hiding anything.

129
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:21,922
They're here for us!

130
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,465
They're here for you.

131
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:25,718
I don't want
any Avatar attention,

132
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:28,972
especially after the Anomaly
showed us Korra's memory.

133
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:31,223
It's <i>because</i> we've seen
what Korra did

134
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:33,183
that we can choose
to be different.

135
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:34,602
And they can help!

136
00:06:34,603 --> 00:06:36,813
That's your life, sis.

137
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:38,690
Not mine.

138
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:43,486
Besides, now's the perfect time
to sneak away.

139
00:06:43,612 --> 00:06:46,906
If we find who made my brooch
and your bracelet,

140
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,992
they might lead us
to Mom and Dad!

141
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:51,035
After everything that's
happened,

142
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:52,661
you're still trying
to find them?

143
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:55,123
I can't stop
when we're so close!

144
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,334
We are <i>not</i> close.

145
00:06:57,459 --> 00:07:00,461
We have a funny symbol that
a jeweler <i>might</i> recognize,

146
00:07:00,462 --> 00:07:02,504
which <i>might</i> lead us
to some artisan

147
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:03,964
who <i>might</i> remember our parents

148
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,090
from years ago.

149
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:06,884
It's a wild
tortoise-goose chase!

150
00:07:06,885 --> 00:07:08,929
We can't just abandon
our parents!

151
00:07:09,054 --> 00:07:11,556
Why not? They abandoned me.

152
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:14,475
And for all we know,
they left you on the streets!

153
00:07:14,476 --> 00:07:18,480
Are you really going
to choose strangers over me?

154
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:22,359
Mom and Dad aren't strangers!

155
00:07:22,484 --> 00:07:24,152
And I'm not choosing.

156
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:26,613
Go then. Who needs you?

157
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:35,538
Come on, Geet.

158
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:43,963
Right now,
my Chancellor needs me.

159
00:07:43,964 --> 00:07:45,130
But perhaps after the summit--

160
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,841
The Summit is the only time

161
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:48,509
our absence won't be noticed.

162
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:51,304
We need to see what
our budding Avatar has learned!

163
00:07:51,429 --> 00:07:53,515
Sorry, Karthik.
It's now or never.

164
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,641
But Nisha's only nine years old!

165
00:07:55,642 --> 00:07:57,727
She's just a child!

166
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:02,481
<i>She</i> can handle anything
you throw at her.

167
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,858
The Avatar is ready.

168
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,453
Where is Karthik?

169
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:19,916
Uh... Something, uh,
important came up.

170
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:21,835
But I'm sure
he'll be right back.

171
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,335
Here you go!

172
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,630
The finest in Elloran cooking.

173
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,090
Save room for dessert!

174
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:29,675
Douhua pudding is coming.

175
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:30,802
Maybe.

176
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:37,183
Thank you all for making
the difficult journey.

177
00:08:38,727 --> 00:08:42,229
Some Havens were unable
to send representatives.

178
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:45,107
And of course,
no word from Republic Forest.

179
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:46,275
- The worst!
- Ugh!

180
00:08:46,276 --> 00:08:47,693
Ellora has contended

181
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:49,862
with threats from all sides.

182
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:50,989
To put it bluntly:

183
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:52,907
we will fall without your help.

184
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:54,409
We need benders.

185
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:56,953
Benders are getting scarce
for all of us.

186
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,873
Yeah, we've got our own
problems to deal with.

187
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:03,043
Tell me what you want
in exchange for helping us.

188
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:05,461
Food.

189
00:09:05,462 --> 00:09:08,964
New Ba Sing Se has experienced
the worst famine

190
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,841
in our long history.

191
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:12,676
We could send benders

192
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:15,554
in exchange
for some of Ellora's harvest.

193
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,015
Yeah, we'd spare benders
for grain.

194
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:21,935
We don't have enough to feed
all our people and all of yours!

195
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:23,353
I may be Empress,

196
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:26,065
but I cannot order the benders
of Feather Mountain

197
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:29,235
to cross the Harshlands
and aid you at their own risk.

198
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:37,327
Nisha doesn't know anything.

199
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:40,412
And this is not a wild
tortoise-goose chase!

200
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,088
Ignore that.

201
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:55,220
Hello? Is anyone here?

202
00:09:55,637 --> 00:09:57,222
Hey, it's beetle kid!

203
00:09:57,347 --> 00:10:00,183
You?!
What's a bug thief doing here?

204
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:02,935
That's "Amow the bug thief"
to you.

205
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:04,895
And I work here...

206
00:10:04,896 --> 00:10:06,439
with my grandma.

207
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:07,690
Is your grandma around?

208
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:10,568
Whoever made this brooch
might know my parents.

209
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:12,987
- Maybe she can--
- Uh...

210
00:10:13,113 --> 00:10:15,948
She's, uh... napping.

211
00:10:15,949 --> 00:10:18,117
But the backroom
has lotsa records.

212
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:20,078
Come on, lets find
your tree thing, quick.

213
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:25,458
Hey! Brigade lackey!

214
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:29,420
It's Daemin, actually. Comfy?

215
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:31,797
If I break these bonds,

216
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:35,217
I'll cook you in a flash,
Daemin.

217
00:10:35,218 --> 00:10:37,011
Mmm, nah.

218
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:39,264
You don't look like you're cruel
for cruelty's sake.

219
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:40,890
You've got purpose.

220
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:46,436
Huh. Well, that's... unexpected.

221
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:52,359
If you expect the unexpected,
you will become bored quickly.

222
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,736
I read that on a wall once.

223
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:55,947
Graffiti can be very wise.

224
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,408
Hmm.

225
00:11:00,285 --> 00:11:01,743
Where's Pavi?

226
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:04,913
She ran off on her own.
Again.

227
00:11:06,249 --> 00:11:08,585
For once her wild nature
helps us.

228
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:10,752
This lot does not need to
know about her just yet--

229
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:11,629
Karthik!

230
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:13,255
Stop coaching the girl.

231
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:15,257
She's gotta stand on her own.

232
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:19,262
The White Lotus cannot risk
another Avatar going rogue.

233
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,473
The Trial will reveal
your spiritual state.

234
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:23,974
Bring it on.

235
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:26,269
- Remember your breathing.
- Hmph...

236
00:11:27,312 --> 00:11:31,900
Despite the chaos around them,
the Avatar must remain centered.

237
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:34,861
They are the eye of our storm.

238
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:41,617
Bend a whirlwind around me
without disturbing this feather.

239
00:12:11,606 --> 00:12:13,274
Excellent, Nisha.

240
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,566
Better than expected.

241
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:17,611
But that was
just the first test.

242
00:12:17,612 --> 00:12:20,073
Let's see how you do with Earth.

243
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:23,408
No, no, nope.

244
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:25,078
No. Nuh--

245
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:27,663
- No!
- Geez!

246
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:29,791
You have weird reactions
to things.

247
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:33,710
Bristlethorn tree!

248
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:36,046
See? That's so weird.

249
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:37,756
Ooh! Gotcha!

250
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:40,509
Says here a pair
of metalworkers <i>way</i> out

251
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:43,262
in the Eastern Outskirts
use this design.

252
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:45,180
They live by a big old tree.

253
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:48,308
Oh! It's the tree
from their sigil!

254
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:51,478
Huh, no one broke a sweat
coming up with that one.

255
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:54,606
Their names are Saumya
and Pramodh.

256
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,697
Saumya and Pramodh.

257
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,240
Mom and Dad!

258
00:13:02,365 --> 00:13:03,908
Wait, I thought you were looking

259
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:07,203
for the folks who were going
to <i>lead</i> you to your parents.

260
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:11,082
No, they <i>are</i> my parents!

261
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:12,791
It makes so much sense!

262
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:15,419
Mom's song
was from the Eastern Outskirts,

263
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:19,798
and Karthik was supposed to find
Nisha in the Eastern Outskirts!

264
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:22,676
He was told to look for her
by a Bristlethorn tree.

265
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:24,386
Like the one on their sigil!

266
00:13:24,387 --> 00:13:26,930
So they were singing
metalworkers?

267
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:28,182
Focus, Amow.

268
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:32,312
Karthik wasn't sent
to a random spot to get Nisha.

269
00:13:32,437 --> 00:13:35,064
He was sent to our home!

270
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,648
Good for you!

271
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:37,983
I think?

272
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:40,194
I didn't follow any of that.

273
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,571
Are we done?

274
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:50,496
To pass this test,
you just gotta hit me.

275
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:52,040
Once.

276
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:53,666
Easy.

277
00:13:58,296 --> 00:13:59,504
Sheesh.

278
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,298
How do you expect
to hit anything

279
00:14:01,299 --> 00:14:02,759
with such a wonky stance?

280
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:10,265
Isn't this your best element?

281
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:20,610
You're losing ground, kid!

282
00:14:26,783 --> 00:14:29,451
You heard me say the goal
was to land a blow, right?

283
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:31,996
Not take a baby nap
on the floor.

284
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:35,165
Too bad, Avatar.

285
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:36,751
Better luck next time.

286
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:38,669
Nisha, no!

287
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:40,463
Hi-ya!

288
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:50,890
You gotta be grounded and steady
to master the elements.

289
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:55,395
A little teasing
made you fly off the handle.

290
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:00,816
Are you alright?

291
00:15:00,817 --> 00:15:02,068
I'm fine.

292
00:15:07,407 --> 00:15:09,324
Would you do me a favor, sunshine?

293
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:12,536
I need you to create a big fire.

294
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:14,830
Now, make the fire

295
00:15:14,831 --> 00:15:17,333
into a small ball, and hold it.

296
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:21,336
Good.

297
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:22,421
Gaze into the flame,

298
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:24,006
and concentrate
on your feelings.

299
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,593
Firebending is fueled
by the emotions which fuel you.

300
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:30,929
Where is your inner heat
coming from?

301
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,932
Is it anger? Frustration?

302
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,600
I just wanted to protect you
from the notion

303
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,271
that your parents didn't think
you belonged with them.

304
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:41,648
Pain?

305
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,525
<i>They abandoned me.</i>

306
00:15:43,526 --> 00:15:45,194
My family!

307
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:49,531
Or is fear at the root of it?

308
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:54,120
<i>We can't just abandon
our parents!</i>

309
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:02,879
Nisha!

310
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:05,964
The Avatar controls
the forces of nature,

311
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:08,842
but that's only useful
if you can control yourself.

312
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:11,471
Sorry, little one. No gold star.

313
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:14,849
There is no need
to take my test.

314
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:17,726
You've proven to be
incredibly volatile.

315
00:16:17,727 --> 00:16:20,353
We cannot risk you continuing
down this path

316
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:21,771
and becoming another Korra.

317
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,276
Nisha passed my test!

318
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:27,152
Surely that's worth something!

319
00:16:27,153 --> 00:16:30,615
It is worth nothing if she
brings a second Cataclysm!

320
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,240
She needs more time!

321
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,909
And she will get it.

322
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:35,536
But not with you.

323
00:16:36,496 --> 00:16:37,662
Wait, what does that mean?

324
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:38,831
It means we're moving you

325
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:40,165
out of Ellora!

326
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:41,334
Giving you a fresh start.

327
00:16:41,751 --> 00:16:43,419
I have to leave my home?!

328
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:46,630
The Avatar used
to move around all the time.

329
00:16:46,631 --> 00:16:50,051
Not having a home base means
you can get rid of...

330
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:52,303
unhelpful attachments.

331
00:16:52,762 --> 00:16:54,388
Nisha's just a child!

332
00:16:54,514 --> 00:16:57,808
You can't take her away from
the only home she's ever known!

333
00:16:57,934 --> 00:17:01,479
You'll push her to become
exactly what you fear!

334
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:05,649
Dragged out here, insulted.

335
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:07,443
What would
our forefathers think?

336
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:10,569
I can't make food appear out of
thin air! I'm not a breadbender!

337
00:17:10,570 --> 00:17:12,615
I wasn't paying attention, so
I dunno what I'm shouting about!

338
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,491
I have something to say!

339
00:17:15,785 --> 00:17:17,912
Oh, that worked!

340
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,246
Uh, well...

341
00:17:19,247 --> 00:17:21,749
I was just thinking that...

342
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,251
...that Havens have always,
you know,

343
00:17:24,252 --> 00:17:26,587
handled problems by themselves.

344
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:29,966
But in Ellora, we know
a single person is no match

345
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:31,132
for the storm.

346
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:34,010
It's only by uniting,
as a squad,

347
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:38,558
as a brigade, as a Haven,
that we've survived.

348
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,768
Jae's right.

349
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:44,813
Separated, our Havens
don't stand a chance.

350
00:17:44,814 --> 00:17:49,025
But together, we can be more
than the sum of our parts.

351
00:17:57,034 --> 00:17:59,160
My people are kind.

352
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:00,538
When I tell them of your plight,

353
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:02,623
some will volunteer
to lend a hand.

354
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:06,876
It might benefit us
to stand with Ellora.

355
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,295
Us too.

356
00:18:08,296 --> 00:18:11,007
But we would still need
something in exchange.

357
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:15,386
I think we can reach
an agreement.

358
00:18:23,311 --> 00:18:25,396
Uki?

359
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:28,941
- Hey, bender! Enjoying the food?
- Not now, Agam.

360
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:38,867
Honored visiting delegates,

361
00:18:38,868 --> 00:18:42,495
council members,
and loyal Ellorans.

362
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,748
We've done the impossible.

363
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:47,043
The Havens will work together!

364
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:49,919
Yeah!

365
00:18:58,346 --> 00:18:59,596
Give it up, Jae.

366
00:18:59,597 --> 00:19:01,473
This doesn't have to be a fight.

367
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,770
Hey!

368
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:13,527
I will end you!

369
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:24,996
All I've ever wanted
is to be a good Avatar.

370
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:28,000
Why is that so hard?

371
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,920
Yeah, I wish Pavi were here too.

372
00:19:31,379 --> 00:19:35,132
You're the first person I've met
that isn't scared of me.

373
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,885
Wanna grab dinner sometime?

374
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:44,641
You are... in jail.

375
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:46,018
I won't be for long.

376
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:49,020
That is a surprisingly
optimistic out--

377
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:50,898
Huh?

378
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:05,579
Guess dinner will have to wait.

379
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,915
Looks like you got everything
you need!

380
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:11,584
Is that your Grandma?
I gotta thank her.

381
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:13,254
Okay, cards on the table.

382
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:14,588
I don't have a grandma.

383
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:16,006
I was robbing the place
when you barged in.

384
00:20:16,132 --> 00:20:18,592
- Hey!
- If I were you, I'd run!

385
00:20:18,718 --> 00:20:19,884
Good luck, kid!

386
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:22,096
By the Havens,
what are you doing?

387
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,056
Get back here!

388
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:25,598
Hmm?

389
00:20:49,457 --> 00:20:51,833
What is that awful noise?

390
00:20:51,834 --> 00:20:53,335
The siren!

391
00:20:54,879 --> 00:20:55,837
It doesn't matter

392
00:20:55,838 --> 00:20:56,964
what the White Lotus thinks.

393
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:58,591
I <i>am</i> a good Avatar!

394
00:20:58,716 --> 00:21:00,468
And Ellora needs me...

395
00:21:00,843 --> 00:21:02,595
- Who are you guys?
- What is this?

396
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,764
- What's going on?
- Are we in danger?

397
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:05,806
Who are these people?

398
00:21:11,729 --> 00:21:13,606
What is the meaning of this?

399
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:23,115
How?

400
00:21:23,866 --> 00:21:26,576
My Queen freed me.

401
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:53,562
Agam?!

402
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:55,647
Hope you enjoyed dinner!

403
00:21:55,648 --> 00:21:58,359
Now, let's chat.

